turin's glory days as an automaker town  have all but faded  the test track for new vehicles used to  be on the roof of the lingotto fiat  plant the building is now a convention  center complex with hotels in a museum  the squares of the old city centre used  to be parking lots now they're  pedestrian zones  the municipal government is trying to  market turin as a center of culture  architecture and design  this striking hall used to serve as a  car showroom for fiat now it's going to  be part of a new university campus  there's been a urban transformation in  terms of  new infrastructure in terms of restoring  of past industrial sites in order to  bring the city from a new perspective  which is  mostly focused over innovation culture  and knowledge economy and in particular  to put torino inside the university city  inside the europe there are already some  100 000 students in turin over 10  percent of the population but the number  is going to increase  the project is aimed to locate a new  public library here in the main pavilion  which is designed by the nervi  architecture to restore the theater  which is now still located here  and to promote the new student rooms for  teaching activity and for faculty here  in the underground pavilion but in this  time of austerity it's proving hard for  turin to come up with the funding for  this hundred million euro project even  so the city offers plenty of  opportunities for young entrepreneurs  like marco guy his industry association  considers turin a fertile place for  business development  young italians have a lot of know-how  creativity and innovative potential  this is expressed in the made in italy  brand which represents a strong  entrepreneurial tradition  and growth is picking up due to their  networking ability both at home and  abroad  large industrial corporations like prima  industry feel they're well positioned  even with less business coming in from  fiat  the parts supply industry in piedmont  still remains very important with 900  companies some 90 000 dependents and  revenues of 18 billion euros only 40  percent of that comes from fiat already  60 percent of our production is for  other customers  it seems despite fiat's retreat and a  prolonged recession turin is  transforming itself into a modern  multifaceted metropolis
 

